  "measurement_note": "Size S is n, the number of trading days, and k = S/8. Legal tiers 8, 32, and 128 span 16x. Repeated four-day blocks alternate profitable normal and short-selling transactions on disjoint day pairs, exercising both open-position states through the transaction limit. The accepted three-state DP is O(nk), which is O(S^2) here. A correct calibrated DP that enumerates every opening day for every closing day is O(kn^2), or O(S^3), and must fail only scaling.",
